This is a Next.js (App Router) + TypeScript project.

Global Engineering Rules:

- Use strict TypeScript.
- Never use "any" unless absolutely unavoidable.
- Follow Next.js App Router conventions.
- Use route handlers (app/api/...) instead of legacy pages/api.
- Keep business logic inside /lib.
- API routes must be thin wrappers only.
- All AI/LLM responses must be validated with Zod schemas.
- Always return structured JSON from LLM calls.
- No UI logic inside API routes.
- Prefer small modular files over large ones.
- Use clear typing for all DB models.
- Code must compile before finishing.
- Avoid overengineering.
- Keep MVP simple and deployable.
- Do not generate unnecessary example/demo components.
- Do not hallucinate external APIs.
- Add TODO comments instead of fake implementations.